{
  "repo": "EH3D-ANDROID-CONTROL",
  "ecosystem": "eh3d",
  "tagline": "The Android app that follows the Bungard machines of a workshop through EH3D-SERVER.",
  "description": "EH3D-ANDROID-CONTROL is an app in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, in the Forge theme of the EH3D programs. It signs in to an EH3D-SERVER, reads the fleet, the jobs and the drill head every second and a half, draws the job in 2D and isometric views with the place of the head, stops a machine (asking twice) or confirms the step a job waits for, shows the camera of the drill head that the server relays, and updates itself from the releases of this project on GitHub. The rules are tested on a computer; the app has not been run on a phone against a real server.",
  "columns": [
    "WHO USES IT",
    "THIS REPOSITORY",
    "WHAT IT TALKS TO"
  ],
